        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3e9df3ee59244e66bf6889e1893b985d",
      "statement": "Flags raised while reading a parsed entry are captured before the per-document try and appended on every one of the four exit paths — unsupported_format, unreadable, processing_error and normal scoring — so a degraded entry never loses its flag by failing early, while on the raw path the list is empty by construction.",
